-- title:
--   Integrality of x⁶j⁴(j-1728)³ when x dj is regular
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$ and a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\Gamma_1(M) \le \Gamma \le \Gamma_0(M)$, and write $K = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$) and $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC` $K\,\Gamma$, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of $K$-series attached to integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ of modular forms of some weight for $\Gamma$, with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g \ne 0$. Let $\bar{j} \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC`, that is $q^{-1}$ times the image over $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-1}$-unit `jNum`, and let $x \in F$ satisfy $x \cdot d\bar{j} \in$ `regularDifferentials`, i.e. for every place $v$ of $F/K$ (a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, not all of $F$, with principal ideal structure) there is $f$ in that valuation subring with $x \cdot d\bar{j} = f \cdot d\pi_v$, $\pi_v$ a uniformiser at $v$. Then $x^6 \bar{j}^4 (\bar{j} - 1728)^3$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra $K[\bar{j}]$ of $F$, and, with $n = [F : K(\bar{j})]$ the $K(\bar{j})$-dimension of $F$, $x^{2n} \bar{j}^{\,n+1} (\bar{j} - 1728)^n$ is integral over $K[\bar{j}^{-1}]$.
--
--   This is the bound on the poles of a differential $x\,dj$ regular at all places of the function field of the modular curve attached to $\Gamma$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, expressed through integrality over the two affine charts $K[j]$ and $K[1/j]$ of the $j$-line; the exponents reflect the ramification indices $3$, $2$ and $n$ above $j = 0$, $j = 1728$ and $j = \infty$. It is used in the identification of regular differentials with cusp forms of weight two and in the resulting bound for the genus of these curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_and_isIntegral_of_smul_D_mem_regularDifferentials_qExpFunctionFieldC.lean

